>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Shenkman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlank</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Shoham</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Borkan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A tale of two exposures: a comparison of two approaches to early clinical exposure</article-title><source>Educ Health (Abingdon)</source><year>2002</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>386</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14741948</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/1357628021000012732</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barzansky</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Berner</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Beckman</surname><given-names>CRR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of a clinical program. Applying the concept of trustworthiness</article-title><source>Eval Health Prof</source><year>1985</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10271783</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/016327878500800205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ilene</surname><given-names>Harris</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What does "the Discovery of Grounded Theory" have to say to medical education?</article-title><source>Adv Health Sci Edu</source><year>2003</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1022657406037</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ilene</surname><given-names>Harris</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Norman GR, van der Vleut